  "description": "TOCJUS crystallizes in the trigonal crystal system with space group P -3 c 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C73 H111 Cu3 Gd6 N3 O40. From the CIF bond table, Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 11 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 11 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 11 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.467-4.160 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.81-116.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd6Cu3(OH)(pdm)3(O2CtBu)9(CO3)4(MeOH)3]·7MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
